From: FlipperEmu
Subject: [PATCH] sd: load a saved state into a card in SPI mode

sd_vmstate_pre_load() powers the card up before its state is loaded,
for a state that has no OCR subsection (the card was powered up when it
was saved). It does so with sd_ocr_powerup(), which asserts that the
card is not powered up yet.

A card in SPI mode is: sd_set_ocr() calls sd_ocr_powerup() for it at
reset, since such a card has no power-up delay that the host could
see. The machine's reset comes before the incoming state, so the load
of any saved state into a machine with an SD card on SPI ends in

  hw/sd/sd.c:409: sd_ocr_powerup: Assertion
  `!FIELD_EX32(sd->ocr, OCR, CARD_POWER_UP)' failed.

Power the card up in pre_load only when it is not powered up already.

Seen with the Flipper Zero machine, whose SD card is on SPI2:
"migrate file:..." wrote a state, and no QEMU started with
"-incoming file:..." got as far as reading it.

Signed-off-by: FlipperEmu
---
--- a/hw/sd/sd.c
+++ b/hw/sd/sd.c
@@ -1067,8 +1067,11 @@
     /* If the OCR state is not included (prior versions, or not
      * needed), then the OCR must be set as powered up. If the OCR state
      * is included, this will be replaced by the state restore.
+     * A card in SPI mode is powered up by its reset already.
      */
-    sd_ocr_powerup(sd);
+    if (!FIELD_EX32(sd->ocr, OCR, CARD_POWER_UP)) {
+        sd_ocr_powerup(sd);
+    }
 
     return 0;
 }
